---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<section class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content">
    <div class="grid mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <header class="section-header col-span-full lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 xl:col-span-8 xl:col-start-3 text-center">
        <h2 class="section-title font-3xl md:font-4xl lg:font-5xl mb-xs md:mb-sm lg:mb-md">
          <span class="font-normal d-block">Implementation</span> Overview
        </h2>
        <p class="section-body md:font-lg lg:font-xl m-0">
          Three steps take an application from an empty project to themed, accessible components
          rendered on the server or in the browser.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="section-features grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-md md:gap-xl">
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-number-one">
          <Fragment slot="title">Install</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Add <code>@chassis-ui/react</code> and its <code>@chassis-ui/css</code> peer with npm.
            Import the Chassis CSS stylesheet once, plus the small companion stylesheet for
            calendars and tables.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>

      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-number-two">
          <Fragment slot="title">Compose</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Import components from the root or a subpath, pass typed props, and reach for
            <code>asChild</code> where a framework's own link or element has to render.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>

      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-number-three">
          <Fragment slot="title">Theme &amp; Ship</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Point the app at your brand's Chassis Tokens, switch dark mode with a data attribute,
            and ship with server-side rendering or the Next.js App Router.
          </Fragment>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
